{"title":"2016 AIME I Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(Similar_to_above_solutions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(Similar to above solutions)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809aa46dd109ae888204a6082a99762896b86a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = (a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> of the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/5597f6815ed01a3ee6f37c93d05a873cc5135a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,\\ldots,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> denote the sum of the three <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e43b6ed51065131d7797ebf783b4e48165667f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1a_2a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93ffc2ad629d9ea686c73b21a52c406a770e1201.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4a_5a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc64d1816c7df22aa5196c4827b09274c5a4c6ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_7a_8a_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> subject to the condition that the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> denote the number of permutations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a46232636e4412d13271a243549da734367cf8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p) = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f61843b083367e905250c95c13cb8942fca2450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|m - n|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) must be in the hundreds places.  For the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the numbers in the ones places must have a sum of either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, since the tens digit contributes more to the final sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> than the ones digit, and we are looking for the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, we take the sum's units digit to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We know that the sum of the numbers in the tens digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f8117b3984bf52b0b798bcee082497545351020c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum\\limits_{i=1}^9 (i) -6-20=45-6-20=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"273\" height=\"50\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4be95305dc6c37da9e700e42113e221ac47dcc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=100\\times6+10\\times19+20=810$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"270\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, realize that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/3920c5e3f6b2e5749cd75c3853b63ae714d00561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> ways of ordering the numbers in each of the places.  Additionally, there are three possibilities for the numbers in the ones place: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3b363b7ac3fc79d6a318291cc107c611a5830d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,7,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/538aff582742c2c683d37644fb78477df27b58de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,7,8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c029e9c3413773190d60ad7c15e92148d6b6788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5,6,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.  Therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94661a77e2b6001676c92513758467459c14836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^3\\times3=648$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" /> ways in total. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdbbbabb757975293908fba43d72fd774a08dbed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|m-n|=|810-648|=\\fbox{162}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like solution 1, to minimize \\( s(p) \\), we must have the hundreds digits to be 1, 2, and 3.\n</p><p>Then, notice that the units digits must sum to 20, as it is impossible to get them to sum to 10 without 1, 2, or 3. Then, we choose the largest numbers to be in the units places to minimize \\( s(p) \\), resulting in us using 9, 7, and 4.\n</p><p>Then, 5, 6, and 8 are in the tens slots, giving us three placeholder numbers, which are 159, 267, and 384, in which \\( 159+267+384 = 810 \\).\n</p><p>To show 810 is the minimum possible notice that we must have the units digits to sum to 20, meaning we carry over a 2. Then, if we assume the middle is less than 21, say 20, then we arrive at a contradiction as we cannot make 20 using any of the others, and thus less than 20 as well is not possible, forcing us to carry over another 2. Then, if we carry over the 2, the smallest possible hundred digits are \\( 1+2+3+2 = 8 \\), and the smallest tens digit is 1 from 21. Thus, our smallest number must be 810.\n</p><p>To find all \\( s(p) = 810 \\), we notice that the 100ds digits must be 1, 2, and 3 (from our proof earlier). In addition, we are to carry over a 2 from the tens places. (one can also see that if we have our 100ds digits \\( a, b, \\) and \\( c \\), then \\( a+b+c = 6 \\) where \\( a \\neq b \\neq c \\) and \\( a,b,c &gt; 0 \\), meaning that we have only \\( 1+2+3 \\) that satisfies the condition). Then, say the middle digits are \\( d, e, \\) and \\( f \\). Then, since we are forced to carry over a 2 from the units digits, we have that \\( d+e+f = 21-2 = 19 \\). Then, we have \\( d,e,f &gt; 1 \\) and \\( d \\neq e \\neq f \\neq 1,2,3 \\). Then, we can do simple casework to obtain only three sets of numbers that work, those being, (4,6,9), (4,7,8), (5,6,8). We then double check the units digits to see if they truly do sum to 20, giving us (5,7,8), (5,6,9), and (4,7,9) respectively, which indeed sum to 20. Thus, we have three possible sums. Each of these three sums has \\( 3! \\times 3! \\times 3! = 6^3 = 216 \\) total permutations within digits, and thus there are \\( 216 \\times 3 = 648 \\) total permutations (which is our value of \\( n \\)).\n</p><p>Thus, \\( |m-n| = |810 - 648| = \\boxed{162} \\).\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28Similar_to_above_solutions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(Similar_to_above_solutions)\">Solution 3(Similar to above solutions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(Similar to above solutions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f7cb9fd71760cbf43a63afec10aef181d77f27b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 + a_6 + a_9 \\equiv 0\\mod 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" />. Since the maximum possible sum of these three digits if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a392ac70771a386bfc02d575630320ca3bb246ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 8 + 7 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> and the minimum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba943173cf5e981d32e9caa2b2a41dd5ef43148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> the only possible values for this sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1000ac18a48346cc72f0a6451d9d54f26b2599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />. Now, intuitively, to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> we need the hundred's digit of the final sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> to be minimized. Thus, the hundred's digits for each of the three summands must be minimized and we intuitively guess <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fafafcb8dbe78fec70b78cd2a2f4a0222372f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. What I'm trying to say here is that we want the largest possible digits to be already used up as the unit's digits so that the smaller digits are left for the larger parts of the sums. So if we want to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> we want to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/2009239e27fdbc99b052e3fa862211f620234071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3, a_6, a_9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> which in turn maximizes the final unit's digit sum. Out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1000ac18a48346cc72f0a6451d9d54f26b2599.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> the maximum sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We established earlier that we wanted to only use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fafafcb8dbe78fec70b78cd2a2f4a0222372f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> as the hundred's digits of each of the summands. Thus we can only use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f0749e4b8e90e7b7017d5636fa6b2948f1aa3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 5, \\cdots, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> as the only digits to sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. There are only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4af63ab7fc2679dc3c5efebf4a014ba53a74f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6, 5, 9), (8, 5, 7), (9, 7, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" /> for the unit's digits. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose the unit's digits row just by choosing any of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ordered triplets and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange each of the numbers within the triplets. Since we fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fafafcb8dbe78fec70b78cd2a2f4a0222372f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> as the hundred's digits there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fafafcb8dbe78fec70b78cd2a2f4a0222372f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> leaving only a fixed triplet for the ten's digits leaving only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" /> ways to arrange these numbers. Ultimately, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf2a590245bdd2befbd455a30f5bbd398d2b3fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3! \\cdot 3! \\cdot 3! \\cdot 3 = 648$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" /> ways to permute to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. The hard part is done and now we just need to find the minimum sum which is very easy. We choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a4af3fd3c3afab561d3c186925b92187c8ac0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9, 7, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> as the unit's digits and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66ce7f76d142a721b5e74cb30696597cc0fde06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 2, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> are our fixed hundred's digits leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baf2184934c577e1418e1e80e0fd5baf8ac7b655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8, 6, 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> as the tens digits. So we have a sum of \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5dba588c1ab667220e85c2822447f1b40debc209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100(1 + 2 + 3) + 10(8 + 6 + 5) + (9 + 7 + 4) = 600 + 190 + 20 = 810$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"542\" height=\"20\" /> as the minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0424fc0fb84e76fe10aa9c29e0206c851a0d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Finally, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/a/29add4ca4061d6073a969992f5bc2632a15220f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|810 - 648| = \\boxed{162}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"152\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WBtMUzgqfwI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WBtMUzgqfwI</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QBHakfd2gnQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QBHakfd2gnQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I\" title=\"2016 AIME I\">2016 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</